zoterostyle-save-as-note =
    .label = Save in Zotero Notes
    .tooltiptext = Create a Zotero entry named 'Addon Item' in Zotero, and create notes under the 'Addon Item' to store reading progress data. If you use this option, be careful not to delete the Addon Item, otherwise the reading progress will be cleared. Therefore, it is recommended to use the 'File' option for storage.
zoterostyle-save-as-file =
    .label = Save in Local JSON File
    .tooltiptext = The reading data will be stored in a JSON file on your local computer. First, create this JSON file on your computer, then click the select button to choose it. Finally, switch from 'Notes' to 'File' (you will not be able to switch if you do not select the JSON file). If you want to synchronize reading progress, create this JSON file in a folder that can be automatically synchronized, select this JSON on multiple devices, and use this option for synchronization.
zoterostyle-Choose = 
    .label = Choose
zoterostyle-Storage-introduce = Reading progress needs to be stored and synchronized across multiple devices. To achieve this, Style provides two storage methods.
zoterostyle-reading-progress-recording-active = Recording reading progress
zoterostyle-reading-progress-recording-paused = Reading progress recording paused
zoterostyle-reading-progress-recording-active-description = While reading PDFs, page and reading time are saved to the selected storage location.
zoterostyle-reading-progress-recording-paused-description = While paused, PDF reading activity is not recorded, and progress notes or JSON data are not created or updated.
zoterostyle-reading-progress-recording-pause = Pause recording
zoterostyle-reading-progress-recording-start = Start recording
zoterostyle-record-time-interval = The time interval recorded while reading (seconds)
zoterostyle-abnormal-fix = Abnormal operation, it is recommended to use fix: 
zoterostyle-fix = 
    .label =Fix
zoterostyle-startup-delay-time = Plugin startup delay time (seconds)

